IMPORTANT CORRECTION: the raw jailed mean FALL from 18.6k (1990) to 11.2k (1996) is OUTLIER-DRIVEN - its bootstrap CI [-31.5k, +7.5k] includes zero and winsorizing turns it into +0.6k. What survives is STAGNATION vs GROWTH: jailed wealth essentially flat (winsorized +0.6k) while non-jailed grew +16.8k (winsorized), so the relative gap kept widening. The literal 'wealth decline' claim is therefore NOT supported and is replaced by 'failure to accumulate'.

